{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>In the second month, on the twentieth of the month.</b> After those who were impure had made the second Passover on the fourteenth of the month, trumpets were made, and by means of them the congregation and the princes assembled to Moses. Scripture then informs us of the order of their journeys by means of the trumpets, and the order of the trumpets in the Sanctuary and in war. And so the cloud was taken up to journey toward Kadesh-barnea — the first city in the land of Israel that they would encounter on that route, which was the way of the great and terrible wilderness, as it says: וַנִּסַּע מֵחֹרֵב וַנֵּלֶךְ אֵת כָּל הַמִּדְבָּר הַגָּדוֹל וְהַנּוֹרָא וַנָּבֹא עַד קָדֵשׁ בַּרְנֵעַ (Deuteronomy 1:19)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:14.622416279Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}